"""A detector of numbers ending in one, strongest for eleven and twenty-one.

The current ASCII digit 1 responds to the preceding digit(s); longer
numbers weaken the response, and a decimal point partly preserves it.
Written eleven, eleventh, and tens-plus-one/first are recognized too,
as are Roman XI and November (month eleven). A formatting response marks the
colon of a document-initial 'Title:' field. Other tokens predict zero.
