Strength depends on whether a root is a bare token, part of a longer token,
or completed across a token boundary. Recent Czech/Polish diacritics help
interpret ambiguous Latin pr. Several r+a continuations have negative signs.
Two formatting cases are modeled too: an initial Title: label, and a document
prefix consisting entirely of middle dots. No semantics are claimed.
